Subject: [CANDIDATE] UML private syscall sites and GS-free runner trampoline

Default off: uml_syscall_patch=1. Work in progress; not correctness-gated.

Writable __access_remote_vm calls restore affected private sites before mmap_lock,
holding the per-mm patch mutex through the write. Single stepping restores all
sites and disables further rewriting in that mm until exec. Guest text readers
(including ptrace and /proc/pid/mem) can observe patched bytes.

The 0x0606xx06 indirect targets leave an invalid opcode at every stopped
MOV boundary in the Go register wrapper. Dynamic RAX is saved under a per-mm
one-try lock before host gettid; contention and lifecycle calls use SIGSYS.
The host gettid exemption matches only lookup instruction offsets, never the
slow syscall. The extra host scratch page is reset before cached-broker reuse.

Alignment-check faults at an exact patched jump restore the mm and retry with
unchanged registers and flags; further rewriting waits until exec. The stub
registers SIGBUS and clears live AC before C; saved guest flags stay intact.

Runner entry rechecks return-to-user work after the patch lease and allocation,
releasing the lease before signal/rseq fixups if either wait scheduled.

